{"step_index":66,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-27T13:26:46Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-27T18:56:46+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-27T18:56:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/priyanshu%20readme/youtube/Stickman/_toolkit/toolkit.md`\nTotal Lines: 270\nTotal Bytes: 16951\nShowing lines 1 to 270\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Priyanshu's YouTube Creator Toolkit\n2: \n3: > Common execution tools extracted from all workflows. Organized by category.\n4: > Each tool includes type, access location, and a short summary of how/where to use it.\n5: \n6: ---\n7: \n8: ## 🤖 AI Models & LLMs\n9: \n10: | Tool | Type | Location / Access |\n11: |---|---|---|\n12: | Gemini (3.1 Pro, 3.5 Flash) | Cloud AI | [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com) or Antigravity IDE — API key |\n13: | Claude / Claude Opus | Cloud AI | [claude.ai](https://claude.ai) or Antigravity IDE — API key |\n14: | ChatGPT | Cloud AI | [chatgpt.com](https://chatgpt.com) — browser or API |\n15: | Groq API | Cloud API | [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com) — API key (`gsk_...`) in `.env` file |\n16: | Google Flow / Gemini Omni Flash | Cloud AI | [flow.google.com](https://flow.google.com) — browser-based video/image generation |\n17: \n18: - **Gemini**: Primary AI for scripting, research, video analysis via `google-genai` API. Use Gemini 3.1 Pro for deep reasoning, 3.5 Flash for speed tasks.\n19: - **Claude Opus**: Script chairman in multi-model council workflows. Strong at long-form narrative structure and critical editing.\n20: - **ChatGPT**: Third voice in 3-model council research. Also used for quick ideation when other models are rate-limited.\n21: - **Groq API**: Runs Llama 3.x at 500–1000 tokens/sec. Use for bulk transcript processing, rapid script rewrites, and batch content repurposing. Free tier has rate limits.\n22: - **Google Flow**: Browser-based batch image/video generation using O\n<truncated 14661 bytes>\n downloads. Often has free PDFs that JSTOR gates.\n244: \n245: ## 🖼️ Image Processing & Visual Forensics\n246: \n247: | Tool | Type | Location / Access |\n248: |---|---|---|\n249: | ImageMagick / magick | CLI tool | `winget install ImageMagick` or [imagemagick.org](https://imagemagick.org) |\n250: | opencv-python | Python library | `pip install opencv-python` |\n251: | librosa | Python library | `pip install librosa` |\n252: | MS Paint | Desktop app | Built into Windows |\n253: \n254: - **ImageMagick**: CLI image manipulation — overlays, transparent backgrounds, batch resizing, Red X overlays, watermarks. Use when Pillow isn't enough or you need batch shell processing.\n255: - **opencv-python**: Advanced frame analysis, face detection for thumbnail selection, sharpness scoring, and video-to-image extraction.\n256: - **librosa**: Audio analysis — pitch detection, tempo extraction, energy contour mapping. Use for syncing visuals to audio beats or analyzing voice characteristics.\n257: - **MS Paint**: Crude illustration reference. Used in stickman/ink style for intentionally rough, hand-drawn aesthetic — the \"anti-polish\" look.\n258: \n259: ## 📊 Competitor Intelligence\n260: \n261: | Tool | Type | Location / Access |\n262: |---|---|---|\n263: | spy_competitor.py | Custom Python script | In your Stickman Studio workflow folder |\n264: | Grok | Cloud AI | [grok.com](https://grok.com) — X/Twitter AI |\n265: | google-genai | Python library | `pip install google-genai` |\n266: \n267: - **spy_competitor.py**: Your custom script for YouTube competitor analysis — channel tracking, outlier detection, keyword gap analysis. Check if it still runs; dependencies and API keys may need refreshing.\n268: - **Grok**: X/Twitter's AI. Used in 3-model council for script generation as a third opinion alongside Gemini and Claude.\n269: - **google-genai**: Gemini Python API. Direct video analysis, transcript processing, and programmatic AI calls from scripts.\n270: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
